{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For all the men.</b> Its sense is: 'if all the men.' And the meaning of the verses is: 'But as I live' — that is, I live and endure forever, and 'the glory of HaShem shall fill all the earth'; if all the men who have seen My glory, etc., shall see the land, etc. — as it were, the matter is not so. And behold, this is the language of an oath, but the expression is deficient out of exaltedness." "<b>And Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote</b> by way of truth: 'But as I live' is a promise to Moses concerning forgiveness. It means that His glory shall fill all the earth through their seed and not through them. The meaning of his words: 'As I live' — Knesset Yisrael speaks, for 'the Life of the worlds,' and He is a living Elohim; He says that the glory of HaShem shall fill all the earth, the lower worlds, and His glory and His mercy shall dwell among them in the land through their seed, but not through them. And this is certainly a promise concerning forgiveness. And it says of Himself 'the glory of HaShem,' as it said (Psalms 104:31): ״יהי כבוד ה' לעולם״." "<b>And you must</b> understand that in every place where you find חי אני, אלהים חיים, and likewise אל חי, and likewise חי ה', all are said of Knesset Yisrael. But when it says (Daniel 12:7) 'and he swore by חי העולם,' that is the great Name. And when it says (I Samuel 1:26) 'חי נפשך,' that is the Place of the vow. And understand this."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "Source cites תהילים ק״ד:ל״א; the verse 'יהי כבוד ה׳ לעולם' is Psalms 104:31. Citation normalized."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:24.988775053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}